# module            why this product does not carry it
# hand-maintained — NOT rewritten by tools/lock-modules.sh
#
# A module named here is one this product deliberately does NOT carry: its logic
# is a local fork inside tools/bootstrap.template.sh, or it serves a channel this
# product does not have. One row per module: the name, then the reason in plain
# words. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored; only the first field is read.
#
# Two pieces of tooling read this file, and between them they close the hole:
#
#   tools/sync-modules.sh  reports the module NOT CARRIED — it is never copied
#                          in (not by the UPDATED path, not by the NEW path) and
#                          never reported "ok".
#   tools/test-modules.sh  exempts it from the INCLUDED gate, which otherwise
#                          fails any module that is locked but @INCLUDEd by no
#                          generated bootstrap.
#
# Without that record, a module sitting unused in tools/modules/ syncs clean
# ("download  v1 == v1  ok") for code that does not ship: upstream fixes a real
# defect and bumps to v2, the operator here sees "v1 -> v2 UPDATED", commits,
# every gate passes — and the shipped bootstrap is unchanged and still carries
# the bug. A row here is a deliberate statement that this product's copy is not
# the code that runs.

download           local fork in tools/bootstrap.template.sh — the shared module builds "umbree-umbree-<os>-<arch>.zip" for a single-component product and would 404 on every real release, and its exhausted-fallback would replace Umbree's $UMBREE_DOWNLOADS_BASE mirror rather than add to it
version-resolve    local fork in tools/bootstrap.template.sh — the shared module's PIN case is hardcoded over Burrowee's four components and fails on anything else, so adopting it would abort EVERY Umbree install; it also asserts a $MIN_VERSION floor this generator never bakes
download-r2-only   Burrowee's private, console-gated relay channel only — Umbree has no gated channel
